760
00:47:27,220 --> 00:47:30,140
Alright next question. I learned black magic.

761
00:47:30,220 --> 00:47:32,220
Hi Junaid sahab.

762
00:47:32,310 --> 00:47:36,280
I want to share something with you that I've never openly discussed with anyone.

763
00:47:36,360 --> 00:47:39,698
I'm not writing this email to seek popularity, sympathy, attention,

764
00:47:39,778 --> 00:47:44,786
or am I particularly interested in whether people believe my story or consider me a liar.

765
00:47:44,866 --> 00:47:46,957
I simply want to hear what you have to say.

766
00:47:47,037 --> 00:47:48,076
I'm in my thirties now.

767
00:47:48,156 --> 00:47:52,255
Around three and a half years ago, I was probably at the lowest point of my life.

768
00:47:52,335 --> 00:47:55,155
My university batchmates were doing well in their careers.

769
00:47:55,235 --> 00:47:56,305
Some had moved abroad.

770
00:47:56,385 --> 00:47:59,480
Some were getting married and others were starting businesses.

771
00:47:59,800 --> 00:48:02,509
Meanwhile, my own little side business had shut down.

772
00:48:02,589 --> 00:48:06,604
My girlfriend had left me and I had an ugly fight with my parents over money.

773
00:48:06,684 --> 00:48:10,354
The argument became so bad that they kicked me out of the house.

774
00:48:10,434 --> 00:48:13,347
I was sleeping on a relative's kitchen floor for a while,

775
00:48:13,427 --> 00:48:15,880
but even there I was made to feel like a burden.

776
00:48:15,960 --> 00:48:20,986
Friends who used to call me their brother only contacted me when they needed something.

777
00:48:21,066 --> 00:48:22,826
I felt like a condom, use and throw.

778
00:48:22,906 --> 00:48:25,550
I was confused, depressed, defeated, and

779
00:48:25,630 --> 00:48:27,557
and ashamed of what I had become.

780
00:48:27,637 --> 00:48:29,279
I had no direction in life.

781
00:48:29,359 --> 00:48:31,001
I started drinking alcohol.

782
00:48:31,081 --> 00:48:36,088
Even though I knew perfectly well that was haram in Islam, but so is black magic.

783
00:48:36,168 --> 00:48:40,921
At that point I had stopped caring about what was right or wrong.

784
00:48:41,001 --> 00:48:44,187
I was just trying to escape my own thoughts.

785
00:48:44,267 --> 00:48:48,301
Eventually I found a menial labor job at a chai hotel in Karachi.

786
00:48:48,381 --> 00:48:52,520
It was nothing respectable in the eyes of my family, but it paid enough.

787
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:56,520
for me to rent a tiny room in a run-down cheap neighborhood.

788
00:48:56,600 --> 00:49:02,520
The room had barely enough space for a mattress, a small cupboard, and a fan that made more noise than air.

789
00:49:02,600 --> 00:49:09,520
But at least it was mine. If there was, it was there that I met a man who changed the direction of my life.

790
00:49:09,600 --> 00:49:11,661
I first met him at a chai hotel.

791
00:49:11,741 --> 00:49:15,542
He was an older man, probably in his late fifties,

792
00:49:15,622 --> 00:49:18,600
who lived somewhere in the same neighborhood.

793
00:49:19,220 --> 00:49:23,020
We exchanged greetings a couple of times before he approached me one evening.

794
00:49:23,100 --> 00:49:25,100
He told me something that I still remember.

795
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:28,616
Beta tumhare chehre par thakan nahi, ghussa nazar aata hai.

796
00:49:28,696 --> 00:49:33,530
Aisa lagta hai tumhare saath kuch bohot bura hua hai aur tum kisi ko bataa bhi nahi sakte.

797
00:49:33,820 --> 00:49:39,020
For the first time in months, I felt that somebody had actually noticed me.

798
00:49:39,360 --> 00:49:41,051
He did not laugh at my situation,

799
00:49:41,131 --> 00:49:44,860
tell me to man up or give me the usual lecture about working harder.

800
00:49:44,940 --> 00:49:45,960
He simply listened.

801
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:48,269
After that we started meeting regularly.

802
00:49:48,349 --> 00:49:50,927
Initially it was once or twice a week.

803
00:49:51,007 --> 00:49:52,500
We would sit at a chaika hotel,

804
00:49:52,580 --> 00:49:56,023
talk about life and sometimes walk around the neighborhood.

805
00:49:56,103 --> 00:49:58,792
Eventually I began visiting him almost every evening.

806
00:49:58,872 --> 00:50:00,698
How I was introduced to black magic?

807
00:50:00,778 --> 00:50:05,018
During our first month our conversations were mostly about spirituality, religion,

808
00:50:05,098 --> 00:50:07,766
human behavior and the concept of the unseen world.

809
00:50:07,846 --> 00:50:13,520
He had a deep interest in traditional occult practices and explained how different cultures had developed their own

810
00:50:13,600 --> 00:50:19,520
methods of seeking hidden knowledge, interpreting events and attempting to influence circumstances.

811
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:25,163
He introduced me to the difference between ordinary religious practices, folk beliefs,

812
00:50:25,243 --> 00:50:29,520
spiritual healing, and what people commonly call Kala Jadu in Pakistan.

813
00:50:29,600 --> 00:50:36,520
He explained that in the local context, people often use several terms interchangeably, even though they do not necessarily mean the same thing.

814
00:50:36,600 --> 00:50:38,600
There was Tawiz involving written.

815
00:50:39,160 --> 00:50:43,965
written in inscriptions or objects believed to carry spiritual significance.

816
00:50:44,045 --> 00:50:49,936
There was Ilm-e-Adad, the interpretation of numbers and their symbolic associations.

817
00:50:50,016 --> 00:50:56,399
There were traditions surrounding Abjad in which Arabic letters are assigned numerical values.

818
00:50:56,479 --> 00:51:02,530
He also discussed Ilm-e-Nujum, or astrology, and the interpretation of dreams,

819
00:51:02,610 --> 00:51:06,420
recurring patterns, and supposedly meaningful coincidences.

820
00:51:07,020 --> 00:51:13,130
He explained that many of these practices existed in different forms across South Asia,

821
00:51:13,210 --> 00:51:15,603
Persia and the wider Islamic world.

822
00:51:15,683 --> 00:51:20,980
Although their origins and religious status varied considerably.

823
00:51:21,060 --> 00:51:27,296
What fascinated me the most was that he did not treat the subject like a collection of random superstitions.

824
00:51:27,376 --> 00:51:31,730
He approached it as a body of traditions with their own terminology, history,

825
00:51:31,810 --> 00:51:33,340
symbolism and internal rules.

826
00:51:33,420 --> 00:51:34,710
During the second month he began.

827
00:51:34,790 --> 00:51:38,948
He began explaining the symbolism associated with Arabic letters,

828
00:51:39,028 --> 00:51:42,040
numerical correspondences, and written diagrams.

829
00:51:42,380 --> 00:51:45,036
He showed me examples of traditional Waqf,

830
00:51:45,116 --> 00:51:50,840
which are square arrangements of numbers or letters found in certain occult manuscripts.

831
00:51:51,090 --> 00:51:56,510
He started teaching me beyond this world's language through which we could communicate to spirits.

832
00:51:56,590 --> 00:52:01,090
He also introduced me to the concept of Hisabe Abjad.

833
00:52:01,520 --> 00:52:06,600
explaining how Arabic letters could be assigned numerically for manipulation of human behavior.

834
00:52:06,680 --> 00:52:12,740
I started maintaining a notebook where I recorded unfamiliar terms, historical references, and the explanations he gave me.

835
00:52:12,820 --> 00:52:19,240
Whenever I encountered a word I did not understand, I would ask him about it during our next meeting.

836
00:52:19,320 --> 00:52:24,980
Some evenings we would spend two or three hours discussing the symbolism behind a particular tradition.

837
00:52:25,060 --> 00:52:29,680
Other evenings he would tell me stories about practitioners he had encountered.

838
00:52:29,760 --> 00:52:30,536
their beliefs,

839
00:52:30,616 --> 00:52:37,880
their methods of interpreting personal circumstances and the importance they attach to secrecy and discipline.

840
00:52:38,060 --> 00:52:43,480
I became increasingly fascinated by the subject, the routine that consumed my life.

841
00:52:43,560 --> 00:52:46,523
By the third month, I was visiting him almost every day.

842
00:52:46,603 --> 00:52:48,402
My routine had become predictable.

843
00:52:48,482 --> 00:52:52,266
I would finish work, return to my room, wash up, buy something to eat,

844
00:52:52,346 --> 00:52:53,775
and then head to his place.

845
00:52:53,855 --> 00:52:57,560
Sometimes we met at the chai hotel, other times we sat in his room.

846
00:52:57,640 --> 00:53:04,560
We spent time discussing astrology and how the concept of date and time and numbers associated in them can be used.

847
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:10,696
He also discussed divination more broadly, including the interpretation of dreams, omens,

848
00:53:10,776 --> 00:53:18,060
and patterns that people believed might offer insight into the future events and how to force yourself into dreams.

849
00:53:18,140 --> 00:53:24,160
Another subject he introduced was the use of unfamiliar scripts, symbolic alphabets, and coded rhymes.

850
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:25,846
writing in occult literature.

851
00:53:25,926 --> 00:53:36,007
I found all of this incredibly interesting because of for because for the first time in my life I felt I was studying something that gave me a sense of purpose.

852
00:53:36,087 --> 00:53:42,234
I was no longer spending every evening drinking or sitting alone in my room thinking about my failures.

853
00:53:42,314 --> 00:53:44,349
I had something to look forward to.

854
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:48,207
By the fourth month I was spending nearly every evening with him.

855
00:53:48,287 --> 00:53:50,496
I usually between one and three hours.

856
00:53:50,576 --> 00:53:51,070
On weekends we

857
00:53:51,150 --> 00:53:58,070
we would start our practical studies and we started practicing influencing human by testing it on animals.

858
00:53:58,150 --> 00:54:06,070
I was becoming more and more obsessed with the idea that I could somehow regain control over my life when curiosity turned into revenge.

859
00:54:06,150 --> 00:54:09,901
By the fifth and sixth months, my interest had changed.

860
00:54:09,981 --> 00:54:12,733
Initially, I wanted to understand the subject.

861
00:54:12,813 --> 00:54:14,070
Now I wanted results.

862
00:54:14,150 --> 00:54:19,150
I started asking questions about whether these practices could influence relationships.

863
00:54:19,330 --> 00:54:24,930
