while doing everything I could to support my mother from a distance.

1376
01:27:50,970 --> 01:27:53,690
Then the story jumps ahead more than a decade.

1377
01:27:53,770 --> 01:27:58,010
By 2022, my mother was visibly and physically older.

1378
01:27:58,090 --> 01:28:02,650
She lived close to my elder sister, although they still did not share a household.

1379
01:28:02,730 --> 01:28:06,970
My sons had grown up. Unfortunately, they had never traveled to India.

1380
01:28:07,050 --> 01:28:11,077
They knew very little about their Indian heritage, and because their mother,

1381
01:28:11,157 --> 01:28:13,786
their grandmother had not been around them physically,

1382
01:28:13,866 --> 01:28:15,660
they never developed the kind of bond.

1383
01:28:15,880 --> 01:28:21,960
I always hoped they would have. That is probably one of the things I regret the most.

1384
01:28:22,040 --> 01:28:28,440
For the past four years we have tried everything we can to bring my mother over on a tourist visa.

1385
01:28:28,520 --> 01:28:31,282
She has been rejected four times.

1386
01:28:31,362 --> 01:28:33,807
I own three houses, Junid Bai, three,

1387
01:28:33,887 --> 01:28:38,000
and yet I cannot have my own mother live in even one of them.

1388
01:28:38,200 --> 01:28:42,580
I've exhausted every option I can think of. Over the past four years I've.

1389
01:28:42,660 --> 01:28:44,593
I've traveled to India three times,

1390
01:28:44,673 --> 01:28:50,220
taking time away from work and doing everything I could to spend as much time with her as possible.

1391
01:28:50,300 --> 01:28:53,500
But there is another thing that makes me feel even more guilty.

1392
01:28:53,580 --> 01:28:58,408
My father-in-law passed away from a heart attack and for the past five years,

1393
01:28:58,488 --> 01:29:02,540
my mother-in-law, who is now in her seventies, has been living with us.

1394
01:29:02,960 --> 01:29:04,567
And sometimes I overthink it.

1395
01:29:04,647 --> 01:29:06,395
I wonder what people would think.

1396
01:29:06,475 --> 01:29:10,180
His wife's mother can live with them, but his own mother cannot.

1397
01:29:10,500 --> 01:29:14,020
And honestly, I don't even know how to answer that question myself.

1398
01:29:14,100 --> 01:29:19,780
Because the truth is I feel guilty. I feel helpless and I feel like I have failed as a son.

1399
01:29:28,500 --> 01:29:33,081
The irony is that I am the same son who grew up watching a single mother raise two children with whatever little she had.

1400
01:29:33,161 --> 01:29:35,037
She worked, she sacrificed, she gave us everything she could.

1401
01:29:35,117 --> 01:29:37,250
And now when she's old and needs her son the most, I cannot give her that.

1402
01:29:37,330 --> 01:29:41,590
gave her that one thing I desperately want to give her, a place in my heart.

1403
01:29:41,670 --> 01:29:45,210
Maybe I am blaming her ego because it is easier than blaming myself.

1404
01:29:45,290 --> 01:29:49,010
Maybe I should have handled things differently in 2011.

1405
01:29:49,090 --> 01:29:54,770
Maybe I should have fought harder or maybe I should have chosen my mother differently.

1406
01:29:54,850 --> 01:29:58,590
Or maybe there was never a perfect solution to begin with.

1407
01:29:58,670 --> 01:30:02,970
But after all these years, I still carry this feeling that somewhere along the way,

1408
01:30:03,050 --> 01:30:03,830
I have failed the woman who.

1409
01:30:03,910 --> 01:30:07,630
who spent her entire life making sure I never failed.

1410
01:30:07,710 --> 01:30:08,054
Junaid,

1411
01:30:08,134 --> 01:30:16,480
I don't know whether I am actually a failed son or whether I am simply a son who got caught between his responsibilities as a husband,

1412
01:30:16,560 --> 01:30:17,630
a father and a son.

1413
01:30:17,710 --> 01:30:25,034
I would generally like to know how you would look at this situation because I have made peace with many things in my life.

1414
01:30:25,114 --> 01:30:28,336
I just haven't figured out how to make peace with this one.

1415
01:30:28,416 --> 01:30:29,710
I am so sad man.

1416
01:30:33,210 --> 01:30:38,690
It's a difficult aspect in life when you have to choose between the two.

1417
01:30:38,770 --> 01:30:41,170
And it often happens after marriage.

1418
01:30:41,970 --> 01:30:43,090
Oh man.

1419
01:30:44,250 --> 01:30:48,194
And especially because your father had passed away very young,

1420
01:30:48,274 --> 01:30:51,090
so you're the only male figure in her life.

1421
01:30:51,170 --> 01:30:55,730
And there's your sister. Like you're only two kids, right? You mentioned.

1422
01:30:56,290 --> 01:30:58,370
So you're the only man in her life.

1423
01:30:58,450 --> 01:31:00,810
But there are technical reasons here.

1424
01:31:01,310 --> 01:31:06,710
So, as you wrote, I think it's a story from the USA, you haven't mentioned cities.

1425
01:31:06,790 --> 01:31:08,790
You said West.

1426
01:31:09,640 --> 01:31:13,491
As far as they are not getting a visa,

1427
01:31:13,571 --> 01:31:26,230
canceling PR means that the country was investing in you and giving you a PR means tax income for them and she wasted it.

1428
01:31:26,310 --> 01:31:27,830
So, they punish for this.

1429
01:31:27,910 --> 01:31:35,270
And the way you are telling the story, I want the overseas to listen to that.

1430
01:31:35,350 --> 01:31:41,860
Like how easy, he moved there, like he got a job from India, he moved to the West,

1431
01:31:41,940 --> 01:31:47,990
found a girl, got married, had a house, called his mother, his mother became a PR.

1432
01:31:48,070 --> 01:31:52,790
So like imagine how different and easy things were 15 years ago.

1433
01:31:52,870 --> 01:31:55,350
And now, God willing, he has three houses.

1434
01:31:56,260 --> 01:32:00,180
And so like yeah, those were the good times man, perhaps.

1435
01:32:00,260 --> 01:32:03,180
And maybe in the next 15 years we'll be calling this a good time.

1436
01:32:03,260 --> 01:32:07,180
People used to come, now they won't be able to come after a point.

1437
01:32:07,260 --> 01:32:13,180
So yeah, it doesn't matter if it's a story in the US, Canada, England, or anywhere.

1438
01:32:13,260 --> 01:32:20,180
But it is sad that you had to make that call and your mom didn't take it nicely.

1439
01:32:20,260 --> 01:32:23,260
Because obviously she will think about it all her life.

1440
01:32:23,360 --> 01:32:27,200
I raised him without a father, this and that, and this is what I get.

1441
01:32:28,040 --> 01:32:34,480
Desi parents are in full ego mode until their body gives in.

1442
01:32:34,560 --> 01:32:36,480
Then comes the poor mood.

1443
01:32:36,560 --> 01:32:39,480
And that's when you start to feel guilty.

1444
01:32:39,560 --> 01:32:43,480
Because until they are walking and working, they don't feel that much.

1445
01:32:43,560 --> 01:32:50,370
Now that thing that you said that they used to get a bell and tea, they have gone there with that practice.

1446
01:32:50,450 --> 01:32:56,370
And she assumed that a daughter-in-law is a daughter-in-law, whether she is white or not so white.

1447
01:32:56,450 --> 01:32:57,812
So tea will come.

1448
01:32:57,892 --> 01:33:01,386
But this is a culture shock,

1449
01:33:01,466 --> 01:33:10,240
our parents don't understand that the smell of pickles or spices in the house,

1450
01:33:10,320 --> 01:33:13,370
they don't tolerate it.

1451
01:33:13,450 --> 01:33:17,830
The reason their mother is able to live because your wife is a…

1452
01:33:17,910 --> 01:33:21,370
is accustomed to her mother and her lifestyle.

1453
01:33:21,450 --> 01:33:27,570
It may not be as intrusive or alien to her.

1454
01:33:27,650 --> 01:33:38,570
But I understand what you're saying that people are thinking that they have kept their mother there and they are like that.

1455
01:33:38,650 --> 01:33:41,570
Boy, I need to.

1456
01:33:41,650 --> 01:33:43,600
Look, your mother.

1457
01:33:43,680 --> 01:33:47,263
She spent a lot of time by herself.

1458
01:33:47,343 --> 01:33:52,760
So she should have understood the importance of family better.

1459
01:33:52,840 --> 01:33:59,130
And maybe she could have taken it nicely when you had suggested that.

1460
01:33:59,210 --> 01:34:06,360
Or I don't know how you frame that in front of your wife or in front of your mother.

1461
01:34:06,440 --> 01:34:10,780
So I don't have that context but I understand from your mom.

1462
01:34:11,140 --> 01:34:17,060
Mom's point of view, because our desi parents, they take everything as an attack.

1463
01:34:17,140 --> 01:34:24,730
That you attacked me, so now the relationship is over, cut everything, divide everything,

1464
01:34:24,810 --> 01:34:26,060
draw a line, etc.

1465
01:34:26,140 --> 01:34:37,140
So your mother didn't take it nicely because her Indian roots perhaps or her South Asian roots were not letting her think logically there and she.

1466
01:34:37,930 --> 01:34:39,930
chose emotions over everything else.

1467
01:34:41,690 --> 01:34:48,810
And clearly your mother-in-law is not a problem because she is from the West and she understands the norms or the way of life.

1468
01:34:51,330 --> 01:34:55,026
Your mom was fairly independent, that's a good part.

1469
01:34:55,106 --> 01:34:58,730
She did the work herself, she took care of you all.

1470
01:34:58,810 --> 01:35:05,010
And then after coming there, she could have been like a typical, most mother that there are.

1471
01:35:05,090 --> 01:35:08,850
I mean not most, I have seen most mothers working there.

1472
01:35:08,930 --> 01:35:11,970
She could have been like, I am sitting at home, my son is earning.

1473
01:35:12,050 --> 01:35:15,970
But one thing she did well, she didn't give up sitting there.

1474
01:35:16,050 --> 01:35:17,770
And she was like, I am going to work.

1475
01:35:17,850 --> 01:35:19,030
And despite her injury.

1476
01:35:19,110 --> 01:35:23,030
Obviously, an old man's injury is long term.

1477
01:35:23,110 --> 01:35:26,030
So she was working there.

1478
01:35:26,110 --> 01:35:31,030
So that's a good thing. That's a positive side.

1479
01:35:31,110 --> 01:35:41,030
But her authority, her authoritative personality, it took the best of her.

1480
01:35:41,110 --> 01:35:44,880
Sometimes some people are good on paper.

1481
01:35:45,120 --> 01:35:50,240
But the behavior, so everything is, I'll give you an example.

1482
01:35:50,320 --> 01:35:54,240
My friend had, like he lived in a big house.

1483
01:35:54,320 --> 01:36:01,320
He had two house helps. There were multiple but like two main house helps who lived in the house with him.

1484
01:36:01,960 --> 01:36:07,559
Now, in that one was educated, could read and write and he had finished his school.

1485
01:36:07,639 --> 01:36:10,903
The other one was not educated at all.

1486
01:36:10,983 --> 01:36:11,283
Okay?

1487
01:36:11,363 --> 01:36:17,150
So naturally he would favor the educated one more.

1488
01:36:17,230 --> 01:36:24,150
He is educated, he is smart, he knows his way around, he knows Google Maps, he understands things.

1489
01:36:24,230 --> 01:36:33,780
Others have to send pictures, like this cigarette, or this brand of shaving foam,

1490
01:36:33,860 --> 01:36:35,150
for example.

1491
01:36:35,230 --> 01:36:39,220
He can't say it, he has to send photos.

1492
01:36:39,540 --> 01:36:41,460
Both of them worked diligently.

1493
01:36:41,540 --> 01:36:42,460
But, what I read was that he was very nosy.

1494
01:36:42,540 --> 01:36:46,460
And that is more…

1495
01:36:46,540 --> 01:36:52,460
He would gossip a lot.

1496
01:36:52,540 --> 01:37:00,460
And obviously, when the neighborhood house helps sit, they discuss.

1497
01:37:00,540 --> 01:37:03,540
The uneducated one, he would keep things to himself.

1498
01:37:07,180 --> 01:37:09,100
He would listen but not speak much.

1499
01:37:09,180 --> 01:37:16,100
Eventually, the way things panned out was that he had to remove what he had studied.

1500
01:37:16,180 --> 01:37:17,087
Because he was,

1501
01:37:17,167 --> 01:37:25,100
he can't become a liability and unsafe because you can't just tell what's inside the house when you go outside.

1502
01:37:25,180 --> 01:37:31,100
Like you never know who is listening, what will he deduce from that, or your security has a problem, etc.

1503
01:37:31,180 --> 01:37:33,180
So, on paper.

1504
01:37:33,550 --> 01:37:36,970
His points were more and he was more handy.

1505
01:37:37,290 --> 01:37:42,430
But it was his behavior that led to his firing.

1506
01:37:42,510 --> 01:37:43,510
Okay?

1507
01:37:44,220 --> 01:37:46,889
So similarly, your mom, fairly independent,

1508
01:37:46,969 --> 01:37:53,290
prefers to be working rather than sitting at home and watching Indian soap dramas.

1509
01:37:53,370 --> 01:37:54,370
Okay?

1510
01:37:54,650 --> 01:37:56,090
These things are on point.

1511
01:37:56,170 --> 01:37:58,290
But the behavior got the best of her.

1512
01:37:58,370 --> 01:38:00,370
You have to be fully packaged.

1513
01:38:00,530 --> 01:38:04,850
So you can't just be, if I'm good at this, I don't have to work on other things.

1514
01:38:04,930 --> 01:38:06,850
Everything has to align.

1515
01:38:06,930 --> 01:38:09,570
So your behavior, the way you approach people.

1516
01:38:09,650 --> 01:38:11,210
I'm talking to everyone.

1517
01:38:11,290 --> 01:38:14,210
That if you're looking for a career,

1518
01:38:14,290 --> 01:38:15,810
it won't work just with a degree.

1519
01:38:15,890 --> 01:38:20,010
Again, I remember this very vividly.

1520
01:38:20,090 --> 01:38:26,010
That I met a gentleman, he had a double MBA, but he was always…

1521
01:38:26,090 --> 01:38:30,610
dirty slippers and cricket trousers.

1522
01:38:30,690 --> 01:38:33,210
And he would roam around in these clothes in the best of places.

1523
01:38:33,290 --> 01:38:36,210
He had his on paper degrees but there was no presentation for it.

1524
01:38:36,290 --> 01:38:39,210
It didn't seem like he was hireable.

1525
01:38:39,290 --> 01:38:42,610
So, just because he has a degree, why isn't he getting a job?

1526
01:38:42,690 --> 01:38:44,610
Your other things are not okay.

1527
01:38:44,690 --> 01:38:46,210
So you have to be a complete package.

1528
01:38:46,290 --> 01:38:48,610
We look for a complete package in our daughters-in-law.

1529
01:38:48,690 --> 01:38:52,090
Beautiful, beautiful, this and that, food comes.

1530
01:38:52,220 --> 01:38:55,980
You're a doctor, but you live at home, etc.

1531
01:38:56,060 --> 01:38:57,980
There needs to be a complete package.

1532
01:38:58,060 --> 01:39:02,380
So if you say on one thing, I'm a good person, that won't work.

1533
01:39:02,460 --> 01:39:04,620
If I'm a decent person, let me run the country.

1534
01:39:04,700 --> 01:39:05,980
No, you need more things.

1535
01:39:06,060 --> 01:39:13,047
So, their authoritative behaviour, that they rang the bell, the tea came, the cart came,

1536
01:39:13,127 --> 01:39:14,460
this doesn't work.

1537
01:39:14,540 --> 01:39:19,900
And, if the light doesn't work with the white light, then…

1538
01:39:20,080 --> 01:39:24,440
Their nostrils are not attuned to those things.

1539
01:39:24,520 --> 01:39:29,760
Our country is very fragrant on a good side and on a bad side.

1540
01:39:29,840 --> 01:39:34,400
So that won't work for them.

1541
01:39:34,480 --> 01:39:36,680
We have smelled incense since childhood.

1542
01:39:36,760 --> 01:39:39,560
During Maghrib, my mother used to light incense in the old house.

1543
01:39:39,640 --> 01:39:40,560
Now she doesn't light it.

1544
01:39:40,640 --> 01:39:43,560
You go to Saddar early in the morning, there is incense from every shop.

1545
01:39:43,640 --> 01:39:46,640
The smell of Metromillan is coming.

1546
01:39:47,180 --> 01:39:53,100
That's why they say that whatever practices you have, keep them to yourself.

1547
01:39:53,180 --> 01:39:53,873
And see,

1548
01:39:53,953 --> 01:40:03,930
the hatred related to migrants is increasing because you don't do your practices on the streets.

1549
01:40:04,180 --> 01:40:06,100
Don't make it other people's problem.

1550
01:40:06,180 --> 01:40:09,100
And it will be good for you to see what they are doing.

1551
01:40:09,180 --> 01:40:11,100
Do you understand?

1552
01:40:11,180 --> 01:40:14,680
Keep it within the confines of your walls.

1553
01:40:14,760 --> 01:40:19,920
Okay, freedom allows you, but then you have to look at the consequences of that freedom.

1554
01:40:20,000 --> 01:40:22,320
What are you doing? How much online hatred is there?

1555
01:40:22,400 --> 01:40:26,360
How many religious processions or videos of protest are there?

1556
01:40:26,440 --> 01:40:28,080
What are they abusing?

1557
01:40:28,160 --> 01:40:30,360
So, when in Rome, behave like Romans.

1558
01:40:30,440 --> 01:40:31,840
That's it.

1559
01:40:31,920 --> 01:40:37,000
So, and the visa, as I told you, that they are rejecting it.

1560
01:40:37,080 --> 01:40:39,920
And that's a simple thing, brother.

1561
01:40:40,000 --> 01:40:42,430
No country is allowed to be old.

1562
01:40:42,510 --> 01:40:47,230
They don't want it because you can be a burden on healthcare.

1563
01:40:47,310 --> 01:40:51,230
So they have so many burdens that they can't take another person.

1564
01:40:51,310 --> 01:40:59,030
So I don't think you're a failed person or a failed son because you made a decision in 2011.

1565
01:40:59,110 --> 01:41:04,430
And its result and emotions and consequences, which are many years later.

1566
01:41:04,510 --> 01:41:08,870
So on that basis, you can't, I know that's why.

1567
01:41:08,950 --> 01:41:14,870
But like, at that time your mother was not old, your mother was not frail.

1568
01:41:14,950 --> 01:41:18,870
I am sure your approach would have been different then, had that been the case.

1569
01:41:18,950 --> 01:41:21,870
If she was eighty years old, you wouldn't have gone to India alone.

1570
01:41:21,950 --> 01:41:24,870
You would have dealt it differently.

1571
01:41:24,950 --> 01:41:32,870
So, with the scenario that was present in 2011, you gave her a solution in that way.

1572
01:41:32,950 --> 01:41:35,390
For sure, its consequences.

1573
01:41:35,470 --> 01:41:39,390
Now your mom is old in India.

1574
01:41:39,470 --> 01:41:45,390
So you thought that but you perhaps didn't think that far ahead.

1575
01:41:45,470 --> 01:41:50,390
Or you didn't know that she would pack her bags and leave for India.

1576
01:41:50,470 --> 01:41:54,390
You probably didn't think that far ahead. Right?

1577
01:41:54,470 --> 01:41:58,390
I wouldn't say that Europe failed.

1578
01:41:58,470 --> 01:42:01,270
And especially your wife, you said your wife was pregnant.

1579
01:42:01,350 --> 01:42:03,270
with your second son.

1580
01:42:03,350 --> 01:42:08,270
So, I mean, there are three sides to your responsibilities.

1581
01:42:08,350 --> 01:42:13,270
Your wife, your upcoming baby, your mother, your career.

1582
01:42:13,350 --> 01:42:20,270
So, like, when there are four ways, then you have to choose only one.

1583
01:42:20,350 --> 01:42:27,270
So, I'm glad you chose your family. Like, nothing against your mom, but then she is also your family.

1584
01:42:27,350 --> 01:42:29,180
And now the immediate family is her.

1585
01:42:29,780 --> 01:42:33,900
I know it's a very slippery slope, where will the mother go alone?

1586
01:42:33,980 --> 01:42:35,900
There is no father.

1587
01:42:35,980 --> 01:42:41,900
But these cross roads that come, you have to choose one.

1588
01:42:41,980 --> 01:42:48,900
So it's a difficult decision. In any case, you choose the mother, the wife goes with the children.

1589
01:42:48,980 --> 01:42:54,900
So today you are sitting in India and emailing that my children have come, I am not able to go, whatever.

1590
01:42:54,980 --> 01:42:57,570
Right? You had to choose one way.

1591
01:42:57,660 --> 01:43:01,000
Now there are three people involved and one person is involved.

1592
01:43:01,080 --> 01:43:04,020
I know nobody trumps the other one.

1593
01:43:04,100 --> 01:43:08,020
Mother is also very important, wife is also very important, and children are also very important.

1594
01:43:08,100 --> 01:43:11,760
These three are very different relations. One can't trump over the other.

1595
01:43:11,840 --> 01:43:16,740
But one decision affects one person and one decision affects three people.

1596
01:43:16,820 --> 01:43:18,740
So you get what I'm saying.

1597
01:43:18,820 --> 01:43:23,820
You did essentially propose a compromise. You gave the other house, right?

1598
01:43:24,630 --> 01:43:25,550
So this was not a wrong decision, it was not a bad decision.

1599
01:43:27,630 --> 01:43:32,550
You could have gone to meet her in the evening, come back from office in the evening, have a cup of tea.

1600
01:43:32,630 --> 01:43:34,550
I know in America, there is not much time.

1601
01:43:34,630 --> 01:43:37,550
You could have found a middle ground.

1602
01:43:37,630 --> 01:43:39,550
You are going on weekends, etc. etc.

1603
