01:58:15,150 --> 01:58:18,190
Also, she joined only nine months ago.

1832
01:58:18,270 --> 01:58:24,790
Also got absorbed into her department and it was higher position than her previous one.

1833
01:58:24,870 --> 01:58:28,350
Now I started thinking that maybe I am doing something wrong.

1834
01:58:28,430 --> 01:58:33,270
Now here he says that there is a sweet showroom.

1835
01:58:33,350 --> 01:58:39,270
I went to my manager and asked him what I should do to get to improve and get promotion.

1836
01:58:39,350 --> 01:58:41,800
He told me that my work is good but I need to improve.

1837
01:58:41,880 --> 01:58:45,070
leadership skills but Junaid Bhai, I am not in a leadership role.

1838
01:58:45,150 --> 01:58:48,371
I said, okay sir, please tell me how can I improve these things?

1839
01:58:48,451 --> 01:58:49,402
He said, we will see.

1840
01:58:49,482 --> 01:58:51,494
Junaid Bhai, I am still waiting for that.

1841
01:58:51,574 --> 01:58:52,163
We will see.

1842
01:58:52,243 --> 01:58:55,857
One thing I have noticed is that whenever there is an important project,

1843
01:58:55,937 --> 01:58:58,279
my manager mostly gives it to these girls.

1844
01:58:58,359 --> 01:59:01,923
If there is any meeting with the regional management, they are invited.

1845
01:59:02,003 --> 01:59:05,435
If there is any presentation, they are asked to prepare for it.

1846
01:59:05,515 --> 01:59:09,080
Meanwhile, I am still doing invoicing, complaints, and updating sheets.

1847
01:59:09,240 --> 01:59:15,320
Last year, our company representatives were invited to a two-day capability showcase conference in Abu Dhabi.

1848
01:59:15,400 --> 01:59:18,240
The company was paying for the hotel, dinner, and activities.

1849
01:59:18,320 --> 01:59:22,640
I was very excited because I have never stayed in a good hotel in Abu Dhabi.

1850
01:59:22,720 --> 01:59:24,920
And thought I will also get some exposure.

1851
01:59:25,000 --> 01:59:28,240
But when the final list came, I was not included.

1852
01:59:28,320 --> 01:59:30,400
My male colleague was also not included.

1853
01:59:30,480 --> 01:59:36,840
Instead, the manager took girl number one, girl number two, and one another female employee.

1854
01:59:36,920 --> 01:59:41,440
There was also one male employee from another department who was very close with the manager.

1855
01:59:41,520 --> 01:59:47,040
When I asked why I was not selected, he said that someone needs to manage office operations also.

1856
01:59:47,120 --> 01:59:49,440
Who will manage the shop behind? He said.

1857
01:59:49,520 --> 01:59:51,640
I accepted it because what else can I do?

1858
01:59:51,720 --> 01:59:56,240
But after coming back, those girls started working on a new project with higher management.

1859
01:59:56,320 --> 01:59:59,440
Girl A was made the project lead after a few weeks.

1860
01:59:59,520 --> 02:00:02,240
Now I am not saying girls should not get promotions.

1861
02:00:02,320 --> 02:00:03,480
If they are good, they should get.

1862
02:00:03,560 --> 02:00:04,673
should get promotion.

1863
02:00:04,753 --> 02:00:07,594
But if I am doing the work and teaching them also,

1864
02:00:07,674 --> 02:00:11,618
then how come they are going ahead and I am still at the same place.

1865
02:00:11,698 --> 02:00:15,585
One day I was talking to another colleague during lunch and I said,

1866
02:00:15,665 --> 02:00:20,916
maybe I should also start wearing better clothes and speaking more confidently in meetings.

1867
02:00:20,996 --> 02:00:24,656
He laughed and said, Arey Bhai, this is not about your clothes.

1868
02:00:24,736 --> 02:00:26,327
You need to become a female.

1869
02:00:26,407 --> 02:00:28,810
My family situation is also not allowing me

1870
02:00:28,890 --> 02:00:31,830
allowing me to take any big risk for job change.

1871
02:00:31,910 --> 02:00:34,115
I send money to Karachi every month.

1872
02:00:34,195 --> 02:00:38,685
My younger sister is getting older and we have to save for her marriage.

1873
02:00:38,765 --> 02:00:45,050
My father is also getting old and his electrical shop is not earning like before because of economy.

1874
02:00:45,620 --> 02:00:51,137
Sometimes I think, you get married, the cleric says, give whatever gift you want,

1875
02:00:51,217 --> 02:00:53,810
give five thousand, give ten thousand.

1876
02:00:54,340 --> 02:00:56,960
It should not be more than that.

1877
02:00:57,460 --> 02:00:59,740
Like, if we only do this.

1878
02:00:59,940 --> 02:01:03,700
Okay, how much did I give the cleric? I gave him ten thousand. That's it.

1879
02:01:04,700 --> 02:01:09,660
There was no expenditure. Because my wife and I agreed that we don't have to spend any more. We didn't.

1880
02:01:10,540 --> 02:01:11,900
It was that simple.

1881
02:01:13,150 --> 02:01:15,413
So we have made it difficult for ourselves.

1882
02:01:15,493 --> 02:01:19,572
Life will be saved, then there will be a wedding, then there will be a loan,

1883
02:01:19,652 --> 02:01:21,020
then to pay off that loan.

1884
02:01:21,180 --> 02:01:26,940
You'll take another loan and then like, so like if people want, it's that simple.

1885
02:01:27,020 --> 02:01:33,180
You have to call a maulvi, get your Naga increased, register it, pick up a copy from Nadra, that's it.

1886
02:01:33,260 --> 02:01:38,060
But no, we have to dance, we have to do this, we have to do that, all activities.

1887
02:01:38,140 --> 02:01:43,740
Because we don't dance. Otherwise, we put it in it, we have to do it in it, whatever.

1888
02:01:43,820 --> 02:01:45,680
Otherwise, we have to do it in our life.

1889
02:01:45,760 --> 02:01:46,671
It's that simple.

1890
02:01:46,751 --> 02:01:51,417
Anyway, so, Economics is a university and I am not very smart like other people.

1891
02:01:51,497 --> 02:01:55,426
Sometimes when I see people speaking English fluently in meetings,

1892
02:01:55,506 --> 02:01:59,770
I feel that maybe I am not made for these corporate jobs.

1893
02:01:59,850 --> 02:02:02,963
Should I complain to HR about my manager's behavior?

1894
02:02:03,043 --> 02:02:07,810
But I am scared that if he finds out, he will make my life difficult in office.

1895
02:02:07,890 --> 02:02:13,240
Also, I don't have any solid proof that he is promoting girls because of personal liking.

1896
02:02:13,560 --> 02:02:16,720
I only have my observations and the examples I have seen.

1897
02:02:16,800 --> 02:02:17,720
That's the email.

1898
02:02:17,800 --> 02:02:20,720
First of all, you have gone from Orangetown.

1899
02:02:20,800 --> 02:02:23,720
Your father has worked hard for you.

1900
02:02:23,800 --> 02:02:25,480
You write really well.

1901
02:02:25,560 --> 02:02:27,980
Up to this point, it's okay.

1902
02:02:28,060 --> 02:02:32,720
Now you have written from AI, whatever skills are required for that, people do not even know how to do this.

1903
02:02:32,800 --> 02:02:36,220
So you write really well, so I am sure you speak also really well.

1904
02:02:36,300 --> 02:02:37,220
Okay.

1905
02:02:37,300 --> 02:02:41,300
Now you noticed a pattern.

1906
02:02:41,520 --> 02:02:50,640
that your boss is giving the girls tasks and giving them operations and you are busy with small tasks.

1907
02:02:50,720 --> 02:02:59,640
Look, you don't have any irrefutable proof for this that you can show HR.

1908
02:02:59,720 --> 02:03:07,720
And your speculation is correct that if the manager becomes more strict on me.

1909
02:03:07,980 --> 02:03:08,980
This is also right.

1910
02:03:09,480 --> 02:03:12,400
And secondly, I will tell you that I have spent three years here.

1911
02:03:12,480 --> 02:03:14,900
If they are not growing, then look somewhere else.

1912
02:03:14,980 --> 02:03:20,900
But having said that, that is also a risk because nowadays Pakistanis are not getting visas.

1913
02:03:20,980 --> 02:03:23,900
So wherever you are in Dubai, make do for now.

1914
02:03:23,980 --> 02:03:30,900
Because recently a friend of mine and her husband, they are moving back because they got the job.

1915
02:03:32,980 --> 02:03:35,840
They were fired from one place because.

1916
02:03:36,230 --> 02:03:37,510
Why? You know why?

1917
02:03:38,470 --> 02:03:41,670
They got another place but they are being rejected for the visa again and again.

1918
02:03:41,750 --> 02:03:43,670
So now they don't have much time.

1919
02:03:43,750 --> 02:03:48,950
They are selling everything and coming back hopefully by the end of this month.

1920
02:03:49,030 --> 02:03:50,070
Sadly.

1921
02:03:50,150 --> 02:03:54,070
They can't do anything but that is there is.

1922
02:03:54,150 --> 02:03:57,110
Now you said that I am not smart, I am not smart.

1923
02:03:57,190 --> 02:04:01,430
Look, this is the job of others to look down on you.

1924
02:04:01,510 --> 02:04:02,600
Why are you looking down on yourself?

1925
02:04:02,680 --> 02:04:07,600
I'm not saying that you should overestimate yourself. That's wrong too.

1926
02:04:07,680 --> 02:04:14,600
You write really well for someone who has a very basic GPA.

1927
02:04:14,680 --> 02:04:22,600
Because I get a lot of emails and I read a lot of messages and comments all day.

1928
02:04:22,680 --> 02:04:27,600
Many people have a language problem. People don't know how to write Urdu. English is a very advanced thing.

1929
02:04:27,680 --> 02:04:29,480
Nowadays people don't know how to write Urdu.

1930
02:04:29,560 --> 02:04:34,480
But I'm not saying that just being English means that you're smart.

1931
02:04:34,560 --> 02:04:38,480
Like I said in the last email that a person should have a full package.

1932
02:04:38,560 --> 02:04:45,480
So pay attention to your things. Try to introspect where you are lagging, how your communications are.

1933
02:04:45,560 --> 02:04:52,480
Or you can ask your boss to give you a challenging task. I'll do one thing and fill up the Excel and keep putting formulas.

1934
02:04:52,560 --> 02:04:56,560
You give me a little challenging task, I think I'm underestimating here.

1935
02:04:56,700 --> 02:04:57,700
Politely.

1936
02:04:57,900 --> 02:05:01,440
Don't say that you have to do this and that.

1937
02:05:01,520 --> 02:05:03,340
Then there is the authority challenge.

1938
02:05:03,420 --> 02:05:08,860
You are doubting me that I am looking at the next gender and promoting it.

1939
02:05:08,940 --> 02:05:13,020
Don't discuss that you did this and that because she came later.

1940
02:05:13,100 --> 02:05:14,700
You only talk about yourself.

1941
02:05:14,780 --> 02:05:17,660
That I think that I have more potential.

1942
02:05:17,740 --> 02:05:22,340
And I am not fully utilized.

1943
02:05:22,690 --> 02:05:26,730
You have to take a task in which if I am overestimating myself, that will also come out.

1944
02:05:26,810 --> 02:05:27,310
If I am not able to do it, then you will be right-proofed.

1945
02:05:28,010 --> 02:05:28,610
And if I am able to do it, then you will be right-proofed.

1946
02:05:28,690 --> 02:05:33,676
And if I do a good job and that is also a learning for you,

1947
02:05:33,756 --> 02:05:40,140
that I can give him more tasks and instead of raising complaints and tickets,

1948
02:05:40,220 --> 02:05:41,610
I can do more work.

1949
02:05:41,690 --> 02:05:44,690
So there is a win-win for both of them.

1950
02:05:50,530 --> 02:05:53,672
So without hiring an additional resource for you,

1951
02:05:53,752 --> 02:05:57,370
you will get more work in the existing resource.

1952
02:05:57,450 --> 02:05:59,370
Frame it like this.

1953
02:05:59,450 --> 02:06:04,330
If you do this and that, that means you are challenging his authority.

1954
02:06:04,410 --> 02:06:09,210
Now look, the boss is simple, he sells himself in front of the girls.

1955
02:06:09,290 --> 02:06:13,690
It's possible that he is like that, he is stubborn, you know.

1956
02:06:13,770 --> 02:06:16,450
Or that he is on some hope.

1957
02:06:16,530 --> 02:06:21,450
You are not in that position. You are in a sensitive country which is very sensitive for Pakistan.

1958
02:06:21,530 --> 02:06:22,450
I have to frame my request in such a way that I can…

1959
02:06:22,530 --> 02:06:26,450
So you have to take every step with a lot of thought.

1960
02:06:26,530 --> 02:06:39,530
You have to frame your request in such a way that I am not going to be a person who is going to be a target of criticism.

1961
02:06:44,500 --> 02:06:46,420
I am not able to meet my potential.

1962
02:06:46,500 --> 02:06:49,420
So I want you to give me a challenging task.

1963
02:06:49,500 --> 02:06:52,420
Because doing one thing is giving me a headache.

1964
02:06:52,500 --> 02:06:55,420
So that is not good for all of us.

1965
02:06:55,500 --> 02:06:58,420
The company will not grow like that and I will also feel the headache.

1966
02:06:58,500 --> 02:07:01,420
And I want to be more test.

1967
02:07:01,500 --> 02:07:05,420
The second thing that is happening with you, there is an example in Urdu.

1968
02:07:05,500 --> 02:07:08,420
He did not get a leave, who remembered the lesson.

1969
02:07:08,500 --> 02:07:11,500
That is, the one who is good at work, gets stuck.

1970
02:07:12,910 --> 02:07:18,830
When I used to do transcription, my quality was very absolute and my speed was very high.

1971
02:07:18,910 --> 02:07:23,830
I used to type with two fingers but I used to type very fast.

1972
02:07:23,910 --> 02:07:27,830
Accuracy, shortcut, your brother's hand was very sad in Word.

1973
02:07:27,910 --> 02:07:32,830
Okay, so because I was reliable, so my bad luck was this.

1974
02:07:32,910 --> 02:07:37,830
Peak MQM time, 2006-2007, there were riots, riots, Benazir incident.

1975
02:07:37,910 --> 02:07:39,645
Oh, I lost in Benazir incident because…

1976
02:07:39,725 --> 02:07:41,645
Because I went to office on foot.

1977
02:07:41,725 --> 02:07:43,645
Because I couldn't work without me.

1978
02:07:43,725 --> 02:07:45,645
So there's no overtime for that.

1979
02:07:45,725 --> 02:07:48,645
The one who is taking leave is taking leave.

1980
02:07:48,725 --> 02:07:52,645
Duray Nayyab has a headache so he is on leave.

1981
02:07:52,725 --> 02:07:56,645
We have to go, we have to work because we are not Nayyab.

1982
02:07:56,725 --> 02:07:57,645
Are you understanding?

1983
02:07:57,725 --> 02:08:04,645
So, for me, this headache became that I am good, that's why I get stuck.

1984
02:08:04,725 --> 02:08:06,725
I never took a vacation.

1985
02:08:07,520 --> 02:08:13,760
Because I never got a leave. We never had that kind of thing. 30 days off in a year. Nothing like that.

1986
02:08:13,840 --> 02:08:19,680
We have to work the whole year. In America, every day a patient is injured or sick. So we work every day.

1987
02:08:19,760 --> 02:08:21,643
I worked 7 days in 3 times.

1988
02:08:21,723 --> 02:08:23,407
In the earthquakes.

1989
02:08:23,487 --> 02:08:26,904
And because we were working on American calendar.

1990
02:08:26,984 --> 02:08:28,727
So Muharram, Ramzan, Eid.

1991
02:08:28,807 --> 02:08:30,400
I worked on all of them.

1992
02:08:30,480 --> 02:08:34,720
So I always got stuck. Always.

1993
02:08:35,370 --> 02:08:39,090
So you are reliable yet invisible.

1994
02:08:39,170 --> 02:08:41,090
You don't have to give growth.

1995
02:08:41,170 --> 02:08:45,590
If you make a manager, then there are four people like me who can make me a manager.

1996
02:08:45,670 --> 02:08:51,890
If you promote, then a good resource, a good worker who picks up good things, will be minused.

1997
02:08:51,970 --> 02:08:54,890
Okay, it will come to the managerial level.

1998
02:08:54,970 --> 02:08:57,890
But then who will work? Labour work.

1999
02:08:57,970 --> 02:09:01,970
You have become reliable yet invisible.

2000
02:09:02,140 --> 02:09:05,060
This is a career loop in people's lives.

2001
02:09:05,140 --> 02:09:08,060
Now again, a slippery slope.

2002
02:09:08,140 --> 02:09:11,060
If you don't become reliable, you'll lose your job.

2003
02:09:11,140 --> 02:09:14,060
The boss will say, you're useless today.

2004
02:09:14,140 --> 02:09:17,060
So this is also a tricky thing.

2005
02:09:17,140 --> 02:09:21,060
That you're reliable enough to have a job.

2006
02:09:21,140 --> 02:09:23,060
Not so much that the person says,

2007
02:09:23,140 --> 02:09:27,060
it's impossible to get a replacement for this, so keep it on this.

2008
02:09:27,140 --> 02:09:29,140
This is a very bad loop.

2009
02:09:30,280 --> 02:09:33,560
So the best thing would be that you request.

2010
02:09:33,880 --> 02:09:37,700
No need to go to HR because you can't prove anything.

2011
02:09:37,780 --> 02:09:40,280
It's your feeling. Fact over feeling.

2012
02:09:40,440 --> 02:09:41,400
Okay?

2013
02:09:41,480 --> 02:09:44,400
Facts are valid in this world, feelings are not valid.

2014
02:09:44,480 --> 02:09:51,980
I think that Ramsha got the job because she has lunch with Sir.

2015
02:09:53,440 --> 02:09:54,880
This won't work.

2016
02:09:55,600 --> 02:09:56,600
Okay?

2017
02:09:56,960 --> 02:09:57,930
So you do what you want.

2018
02:09:58,010 --> 02:10:03,930
In normal circumstances, if you are challenged and you don't get it, say Salam and go to the next job.

2019
02:10:04,010 --> 02:10:10,930
But if you are in a place where the Pakistani visa is being rejected, I am not saying this to scare you, I am saying this factually.

2020
02:10:11,010 --> 02:10:17,930
If you leave your job because of me, even if you get it next time, you can cancel your visa and then what will you do?

2021
02:10:18,010 --> 02:10:25,010
So I don't want you to come back to Orangetown and sit at the electric shop.

2022
02:10:25,190 --> 02:10:32,110
So somehow stay in that but you can voice yourself politely.

2023
02:10:32,190 --> 02:10:40,110
And if you don't talk to the manager then you have to keep the same framing in HR that I am not doing what I can.

2024
02:10:40,190 --> 02:10:46,366
So please ensure that I get the right challenge.

2025
02:10:46,446 --> 02:10:49,106
Do you understand?

2026
02:10:49,186 --> 02:10:50,190
Do this.

2027
02:10:51,550 --> 02:10:55,594
Do not create doubts, do not blame anyone.

2028
02:10:55,674 --> 02:10:59,270
Avoid this because they will go downhill.

2029
02:10:59,350 --> 02:11:03,207
Rest, the projects and presentations that you have written, again,

2030
02:11:03,287 --> 02:11:06,880
100% those who are going to conferences and taking pictures,

2031
02:11:06,960 --> 02:11:09,077
they are looking at the presentation,

2032
02:11:09,157 --> 02:11:12,270
the presentation is looking at the higher management.

2033
02:11:12,350 --> 02:11:16,350
The one who is filing and taking out the photocopy is doing this and that.

2034
02:11:16,940 --> 02:11:19,460
You have to be in a role that makes you visible.

2035
02:11:19,540 --> 02:11:22,300
So this again…

2036
02:11:22,380 --> 02:11:33,460
You have to be seen in the pictures, in the newsletters, in the emails, in the praise.

2037
02:11:33,540 --> 02:11:37,300
These are the things that you have to ask for.

2038
02:11:37,380 --> 02:11:42,180
The other thing that your manager said that you need leadership skills and we'll see.

2039
02:11:44,770 --> 02:11:48,590
It's a matter of time. We'll see. There's a deadline.

2040
02:11:48,670 --> 02:11:52,090
Vague things cannot work in corporate.

2041
02:11:52,170 --> 02:11:55,090
It has to be like, I'm looking at this point.

2042
02:11:55,170 --> 02:12:00,390
That we will review or we can set up a team.

2043
02:12:00,470 --> 02:12:09,390
So we'll see if it's not a valuable feedback in my opinion.

2044
02:12:09,470 --> 02:12:11,840
And what you said.

2045
02:12:11,920 --> 02:12:13,840
Why haven't I been promoted?

2046
02:12:13,920 --> 02:12:15,840
Put this frame aside.

2047
02:12:15,920 --> 02:12:17,840
Say it like this.

2048
02:12:17,920 --> 02:12:21,840
That for the next 6 months, I need a measurable challenge.

2049
02:12:21,920 --> 02:12:23,840
So give me a challenge.

2050
02:12:23,920 --> 02:12:28,840
Or give me a project or presentation.

2051
02:12:28,920 --> 02:12:31,840
Any monthly report or sales report or anything.

2052
02:12:31,920 --> 02:12:33,840
Give me a chance. I would like to present.

2053
02:12:33,920 --> 02:12:36,840
This is how I will learn. This is how I will gain.

2054
02:12:36,920 --> 02:12:38,920
I will not learn by going to the next job.

2055
02:12:39,280 --> 02:12:41,200
Learn this on this job.

2056
02:12:41,280 --> 02:12:43,200
If you take any task, you document it.

2057
02:12:43,280 --> 02:12:45,200
And make sure it's in email form.

2058
02:12:45,280 --> 02:12:52,200
That on such and such date, you gave me this task, I took these measures and this result came out.

2059
02:12:52,280 --> 02:12:55,200
A, I got the task, B I did this, C this result.

2060
02:12:55,280 --> 02:12:58,200
So A, B, C formula, which I just created with myself.

2061
02:12:58,280 --> 02:13:01,200
Talk by doing A, B, C.

2062
02:13:01,280 --> 02:13:05,200
Don't go to HR and say that they are promoting girls and not me.

2063
02:13:05,280 --> 02:13:06,280
Don't do this.

2064
02:13:06,760 --> 02:13:10,180
Nobody would take it nicely. I can tell you that.

2065
02:13:10,260 --> 02:13:14,180
So that's all I have to say.

2066
02:13:14,260 --> 02:13:19,180
Don't quit recklessly. Jobs are very difficult right now.

2067
02:13:19,260 --> 02:13:22,180
In the country you are in, it is very difficult.

2068
02:13:22,260 --> 02:13:24,180
And there, for us, visas are also very difficult.

2069
02:13:24,260 --> 02:13:30,180
So I hope you will make a logical decision.

2070
02:13:30,260 --> 02:13:32,680
And play it strategically.

2071
02:13:32,760 --> 02:13:33,860
See, this is the scene of corporate.

2072
02:13:33,940 --> 02:13:41,860
It has to be very strategic and you have to work with a lot of respect and be a good person.

2073
02:13:41,940 --> 02:13:49,594
Talent doesn't always trump personal liking, relationship, who smokes with the boss,

2074
02:13:49,674 --> 02:13:52,860
this is a big thing in today's world.

2075
02:13:52,940 --> 02:13:57,858
One of our friends, why did he get a promotion?

2076
02:13:57,938 --> 02:14:00,800
Because he plays golf with the CEO at 6 AM.

2077
02:14:00,880 --> 02:14:04,240
So what you do after hours is also working.

2078
02:14:04,560 --> 02:14:05,700
It's also work.

2079
02:14:06,200 --> 02:14:08,060
Go out with your boss.

2080
02:14:08,500 --> 02:14:12,260
I'm not saying pick up, but that's the scene.

2081
02:14:12,340 --> 02:14:13,600
Stay in your eyes.

2082
02:14:13,680 --> 02:14:16,740
They disappeared with the task and did the work and gave it back.

2083
02:14:17,020 --> 02:14:21,580
Look around a little, socialize a little and learn the craft.

2084
02:14:22,240 --> 02:14:27,860
Rest, don't undermine yourself like I'm not smart. You're smart.

2085
02:14:28,290 --> 02:14:35,130
You're stuck in a loop, so your smartness or lack thereof is not the reason.

2086
02:14:35,210 --> 02:14:37,810
It's clearly something else.

2087
02:14:37,890 --> 02:14:41,290
So I hope you treat it logically.

2088
02:14:41,370 --> 02:14:42,210
Take care.

2089
02:14:55,430 --> 02:15:01,738
asset which I'm hoping to eventually turn into something I can sell to multiple buyers through tech sales.

2090
02:15:01,818 --> 02:15:04,156
I mentioned this because I was working.

2091
02:15:04,236 --> 02:15:10,970
I heard one of the answers from the sister who keeps visiting her brother unannounced in the middle of the day.

2092
02:15:11,050 --> 02:15:14,167
And the answer genuinely got me thinking about something.

2093
02:15:14,247 --> 02:15:15,632
Why are our people so far?

2094
02:15:15,712 --> 02:15:21,800
I will start with my own family because I don't want to make this a lecture about everyone else while pretending

2095
02:15:21,880 --> 02:15:24,181
pretending my own house is different.

2096
02:15:24,261 --> 02:15:27,145
My mother has a physical disability, so unfortunately,

2097
02:15:27,225 --> 02:15:29,798
she never had the opportunity to work.

2098
02:15:29,878 --> 02:15:33,230
But even in my own generation, I see something that bothers me.

2099
02:15:33,310 --> 02:15:36,609
All three of my sisters are married now and none of them work.

2100
02:15:36,689 --> 02:15:40,559
They have their committee parties, birthday parties, anniversary parties,

2101
02:15:40,639 --> 02:15:45,029
and a million other social commitments that somehow keep appearing on the calendar.

2102
02:15:45,109 --> 02:15:47,250
Their week can genuinely be spent deciding

2103
02:15:47,330 --> 02:15:49,963
deciding what clothes to wear to the next party.

2104
02:15:50,043 --> 02:15:58,655
And the other one or two days they have free from this free time from this incredibly busy social calendar are sometimes spent on ballot committee.

2105
02:15:58,735 --> 02:15:59,642
Meanwhile, I'm 27.

2106
02:15:59,722 --> 02:16:04,819
I work two jobs and I have a passion project on the side which I have very high hopes for.

2107
02:16:04,899 --> 02:16:06,983
And the strange thing is, Junaid Bhai,

2108
02:16:07,063 --> 02:16:11,830
I don't work this much because something is forcing me to somebody is forcing me to.

2109
02:16:11,910 --> 02:16:13,366
I actually enjoy being busy.

2110
02:16:13,446 --> 02:16:13,746
There

2111
02:16:13,826 --> 02:16:19,618
There is something incredibly satisfying about waking up and knowing you have something to build,

2112
02:16:19,698 --> 02:16:23,000
something to learn, something to sell, something to improve.

2113
02:16:23,080 --> 02:16:24,399
And then I look around.

2114
02:16:24,479 --> 02:16:27,347
Most of my relatives are planning to study abroad.

2115
02:16:27,427 --> 02:16:29,148
Emphasis on the word planning.

2116
02:16:29,228 --> 02:16:33,840
I generally think the word planning was invented for them during COVID in 2020.

2117
02:16:33,920 --> 02:16:39,725
There are seven people I regularly talk to who have been planning to go abroad for years.

2118
02:16:39,805 --> 02:16:41,010
Not one of them works.

2119
02:16:41,090 --> 02:16:44,290
And whenever the topic comes up, the answer is always the same.

2120
02:16:44,370 --> 02:16:49,210
We'll go out and do anything. We'll drive Uber. We'll make a burger at McDonald's. We'll drive a cab.

2121
02:16:49,290 --> 02:16:53,090
And I always want to ask them, why not in Pakistan?

2122
02:16:53,170 --> 02:16:57,250
If you are genuinely willing to work when you land abroad, why are you sitting at home here?

2123
02:16:57,330 --> 02:17:00,878
If driving a cab is respectable work in Australia, Canada or the UK,

2124
02:17:00,958 --> 02:17:04,930
why does it suddenly become beneath you in Lahore, Karachi or Islamabad?

2125
02:17:05,010 --> 02:17:06,850
And then I look at my neighborhood.

2126
02:17:08,100 --> 02:17:12,820
around us that basically function as miniature social clubs. Ludo is being played, cricket

2127
02:17:12,900 --> 02:17:17,100
or the news is running on television and five or six people are sitting around having

2128
02:17:17,180 --> 02:17:21,380
a very serious discussion about the one person who has single-handedly destroyed

2129
02:17:21,460 --> 02:17:25,980
Pakistan. The funny thing is you can replace the word politician with a cricketer and

2130
02:17:26,060 --> 02:17:31,140
the entire argument still works. And this is where I started wondering whether we sometimes

2131
02:17:31,220 --> 02:17:35,820
use unemployment as an explanation for something that is actually much more complicated.

2132
02:17:36,160 --> 02:17:39,960
Because yes, Pakistan absolutely has an unemployment problem.

2133
02:17:40,040 --> 02:17:46,180
The latest Pakistan Bureau of Statistics Labour Force Survey 2024-25 puts unemployment

2134
02:17:46,260 --> 02:17:48,500
at 7.1%.

2135
02:17:48,580 --> 02:17:51,840
That is around 5.9 million people who are unemployed.

2136
02:17:51,920 --> 02:18:03,270
The Labour Force is about 83.1 million and around 77.2 million people are employed under the new 19th ICLS definition.

2137
02:18:03,350 --> 02:18:04,470
I don't know what that is.

2138
02:18:04,550 --> 02:18:06,970
There is also a pretty serious provincial disparity.

2139
02:18:07,050 --> 02:18:14,431
Khyber Pakhtunkhwa has the highest unemployment rate at 9.6%, followed by Punjab at 7.3%,

2140
02:18:14,511 --> 02:18:17,800
Balochistan at 5.5%, and Sindh at 5.3%.

2141
02:18:17,910 --> 02:18:20,150
And the youth numbers are even more worrying.

2142
02:18:20,230 --> 02:18:25,089
Among 15 to 24 years old, around 2.6 million people are unemployed,

2143
02:18:25,169 --> 02:18:29,510
and another 25.8 million are outside the labor force.

2144
02:18:29,590 --> 02:18:31,340
The youth unemployment rate is around.

2145
02:18:31,420 --> 02:18:32,298
around 12.8%.

2146
02:18:32,378 --> 02:18:37,993
But the statistics that really caught my attention was the need figure.

2147
02:18:38,073 --> 02:18:42,208
Around 28.4% of Pakistan's 15 to 24 year olds are need,

2148
02:18:42,288 --> 02:18:46,645
meaning they are not in employment, education or training.

2149
02:18:46,725 --> 02:18:55,406
That is nearly three out of every 10 young people and the provincial differences are quite stark as well.

2150
02:18:55,486 --> 02:18:59,360
Youth need is 24.8% in Punjab, 32 in Sindh, 32.7 Kp.

2151
02:18:59,440 --> 02:19:00,392
36% in Balochistan.

2152
02:19:00,472 --> 02:19:05,745
Now before someone tells me that these people are all lazy, I want to be careful here.

2153
02:19:05,825 --> 02:19:06,451
They are not.

2154
02:19:06,531 --> 02:19:09,573
And this is where I think the conversation needs nuance.

2155
02:19:09,653 --> 02:19:16,813
Unemployment technically refers to people who are part of the labor force and are looking for work but don't have a job.

2156
02:19:16,893 --> 02:19:21,077
Someone who isn't looking for work isn't automatically counted as unemployed.

2157
02:19:21,157 --> 02:19:23,493
So there are really two different problems.

2158
02:19:23,573 --> 02:19:25,500
There is involuntary unemployment.

2159
02:19:25,700 --> 02:19:29,220
I want to work, I am available to work but I cannot find a job.

2160
02:19:29,300 --> 02:19:34,980
Okay, this is one and then there is voluntary or structural non-participation.

2161
02:19:35,060 --> 02:19:38,900
I am not working and I am not actively trying to enter the labor market.

2162
02:19:38,980 --> 02:19:46,980
The official statistics do not give us a proper number called voluntary unemployment because that is not how unemployment is defined.

2163
02:19:47,060 --> 02:19:50,970
But that does not mean the second problem does not exist. In fact, the size of the population.

2164
02:19:51,050 --> 02:19:56,970
outside the labor force shows just how important the equation, the question is.

2165
02:19:57,050 --> 02:20:03,050
And this is where I want to come back to my original question. Why are our people so far in?

2166
02:20:03,140 --> 02:20:07,678
Imagine, Junaid Bhai, that tomorrow some Kudrat ka Nizam happens,

2167
02:20:07,758 --> 02:20:11,735
China gets hit by a zombie apocalypse, India gets flooded,

2168
02:20:11,815 --> 02:20:17,050
Southeast Asia gets hit with a tsunami, Mexico gets wiped out by a meteor.

2169
02:20:17,690 --> 02:20:21,672
And somehow, magically the entire world's manufacturing moves to Pakistan.

2170
02:20:21,752 --> 02:20:25,808
Certainly factories are everywhere, textile mills are running,

2171
02:20:25,888 --> 02:20:30,650
electronics are being assembled, cars are being manufactured, warehouses are operating,

2172
02:20:30,730 --> 02:20:31,887
ports are moving goods,

2173
02:20:31,967 --> 02:20:38,477
foreign companies are opening plants and somehow miraculously our political leadership also manages to not mess it up.

2174
02:20:38,557 --> 02:20:42,565
Let's even assume that they solved the conventional unemployment problem.

2175
02:20:42,645 --> 02:20:44,950
Every person who genuinely wants a job

2176
02:20:45,030 --> 02:20:46,042
wants a job gets one.

2177
02:20:46,122 --> 02:20:46,511
Now what?

2178
02:20:46,591 --> 02:20:48,567
What do we do about the other problem?

2179
02:20:48,647 --> 02:20:55,754
How do you fix a culture where somebody can spend three or four years planning to leave the country without working in the meantime?

2180
02:20:55,834 --> 02:21:04,585
How do you convince a young man sitting at a dhaba every afternoon that learning a skill is better than spending six hours discussing Babar Azam's strike rate?

2181
02:21:04,665 --> 02:21:09,819
How do you convince families that a son or a daughter doesn't need to wait for a government job,

2182
02:21:09,899 --> 02:21:12,520
an overseas visa or a perfect career opportunity before

2183
02:21:12,600 --> 02:21:19,620
before starting to contribute and perhaps most importantly how do we make work aspirational again.

2184
02:21:19,700 --> 02:21:23,220
Because I don't think Pakistan's problem is simply that there aren't enough jobs.

2185
02:21:23,300 --> 02:21:28,320
That is obviously a massive problem. But even if tomorrow you magically created millions of jobs,

2186
02:21:28,400 --> 02:21:34,620
I don't think the problem would disappear completely. We would still have to answer a much harder question.

2187
02:21:34,700 --> 02:21:40,780
How do you create a society where people actually want to be productive, where I'm I'm busy building.

2188
02:21:40,860 --> 02:21:43,761
something is a better status symbol than I'm free all day.

2189
02:21:43,841 --> 02:21:52,264
Where doing a small job in Pakistan is not considered embarrassing while doing the exact same job abroad is considered an achievement.

2190
02:21:52,344 --> 02:22:00,307
Where a twenty-four year old isn't spending his best years waiting for bahar jane ka scene to happen and where being far-right isn't treated as a lifestyle.

2191
02:22:00,387 --> 02:22:02,818
I genuinely don't have the answer, Junaid Bhai,

2192
02:22:02,898 --> 02:22:06,149
but after hearing that episode I couldn't stop thinking about it.

2193
02:22:06,229 --> 02:22:07,940
Maybe this is a bigger problem than

2194
02:22:08,020 --> 02:22:09,394
than unemployment.

2195
02:22:09,474 --> 02:22:12,300
Maybe we don't just need more jobs.

2196
02:22:12,380 --> 02:22:16,740
Maybe we need a culture of work, regards and respect.

2197
02:22:16,820 --> 02:22:18,235
Very good question, man.

2198
02:22:18,315 --> 02:22:21,793
This is absolutely a brilliant question and an observation.

2199
02:22:21,873 --> 02:22:22,442
Absolutely,

2200
02:22:22,522 --> 02:22:27,929
you are right that there is involuntary unemployment and there is voluntary unemployment.

2201
02:22:28,009 --> 02:22:29,660
I don't want to work at all.

2202
02:22:29,820 --> 02:22:35,820
Like you gave an example of that sister-in-law, that sister who comes home every day.

2203
02:22:36,350 --> 02:22:41,405
I'm not going to deny, as we discussed in the last episode,

2204
02:22:41,485 --> 02:22:44,790
how much the female doctor had to face.

2205
02:22:44,870 --> 02:22:50,630
If we talk about work culture, then women are in very miserable situations.

2206
02:22:50,710 --> 02:22:52,950
There is no denying that.

2207
02:22:53,030 --> 02:23:02,230
Having said that, at the same time, there is a rampant mindset among women who…

2208
02:23:02,310 --> 02:23:03,730
Who just don't want to work?

2209
02:23:03,810 --> 02:23:06,930
Now, should all women work?

2210
02:23:07,010 --> 02:23:10,430
Or can they? Or will they? No.

2211
02:23:10,510 --> 02:23:15,030
Obviously, some people chose to be a working housewife.

2212
02:23:15,110 --> 02:23:16,630
And that's perfectly fine.

2213
02:23:16,710 --> 02:23:21,030
But then, even in that, how involved are you with?

2214
02:23:21,110 --> 02:23:25,030
Hey, like, I'm saying that if you want to be a working housewife, so are you doing that?

2215
02:23:25,110 --> 02:23:26,630
She's doing all the work.

2216
02:23:26,710 --> 02:23:28,230
He's doing the cleaner, he's doing this, he's doing that.

2217
02:23:28,310 --> 02:23:30,080
What are you actually doing other?

2218
02:23:30,160 --> 02:23:32,640
other than running an order, do this, do that.

2219
02:23:32,720 --> 02:23:37,000
Either you are personally involved, you are driving your kids to school,

2220
02:23:37,080 --> 02:23:43,160
bringing them back, taking them for tuitions, bringing them back, taking them for sports, or Maulvi Sahib.

2221
02:23:43,240 --> 02:23:47,160
So like your day is also fully engaged around your kids.

2222
02:23:47,240 --> 02:23:49,560
That's the part I understand.

2223
02:23:49,840 --> 02:23:56,426
But if you have outsourced everything so that the madam gets ready and does coffee outings every day,

2224
02:23:56,506 --> 02:23:58,160
that is, I don't know man.

2225
02:23:58,360 --> 02:24:01,040
So that is an observation.

2226
02:24:01,120 --> 02:24:03,840
Other than that, if we talk about it,

2227
02:24:03,920 --> 02:24:07,480
we have a lot of voluntary unemployment.

2228
02:24:07,560 --> 02:24:09,480
That we don't have to work.

2229
02:24:09,560 --> 02:24:12,040
I knew a group of people back in the day,

2230
02:24:12,120 --> 02:24:17,200
who were unemployed for 8 years voluntarily for this reason.

2231
02:24:17,280 --> 02:24:19,960
There were lands behind, etc.

2232
02:24:20,040 --> 02:24:23,440
That when Benazir Sahiba comes, she will get a job in PIA.

2233
02:24:23,520 --> 02:24:24,520
Okay?

2234
02:24:24,830 --> 02:24:27,750
They spent 8 years of their youth in this prison.

2235
02:24:27,830 --> 02:24:30,750
When Benazir came, she died.

2236
02:24:30,830 --> 02:24:38,750
She sat there and then all the lands were sold slowly and then they faced a lot of hardships.

2237
02:24:38,830 --> 02:24:42,809
We have a complete Nawabi culture, false claims of respect,

2238
02:24:42,889 --> 02:24:48,750
which you can say that they will do all the work outside but not here.

2239
02:24:48,830 --> 02:24:52,830
Work is work, but we have a social hierarchy.

2240
02:24:52,920 --> 02:24:53,930
There is a reason.

2241
02:24:54,010 --> 02:24:59,348
India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, even in India if we talk about North India,

2242
02:24:59,428 --> 02:25:01,008
why is it so dirty?

2243
02:25:01,088 --> 02:25:07,640
Because of the Nawabi culture that I am upper caste and cleanliness is the job of the lower caste.

2244
02:25:07,720 --> 02:25:10,514
In our country, you can see all the recruitment.

2245
02:25:10,594 --> 02:25:15,720
How shamelessly it is in the newspapers even today that non-Muslim cleaner is needed.

2246
02:25:20,200 --> 02:25:26,120
The Hadith says that cleanliness is half-hearted. To clean the floor, you don't need a Muslim. You need a Hindu or a Christian.

2247
02:25:26,200 --> 02:25:29,075
So, it's the same thing in the newspaper.

2248
02:25:29,155 --> 02:25:32,038
You can see it and it's not something that's new.

2249
02:25:32,118 --> 02:25:34,120
We've been seeing it for centuries.

2250
02:25:34,200 --> 02:25:38,842
So, work is work, but certain work is for certain people.

2251
02:25:38,922 --> 02:25:43,120
This work is for certain people, this work is for certain people.

2252
02:25:43,200 --> 02:25:47,970
So, where you create this kind of hierarchy, you create an element of shame.

2253
02:25:48,050 --> 02:25:50,485
When you create an element of shame,

2254
02:25:50,565 --> 02:25:59,760
you will be a witness of this yourself if you have used Uber or Kareem in Pakistan or you have used services in Pakistan.

2255
02:26:00,690 --> 02:26:05,586
Many people get offended if you sit behind because they don't want to be like, oh,

2256
02:26:05,666 --> 02:26:07,610
I am not your driver, so what are you?

2257
02:26:07,690 --> 02:26:12,850
You are driving a car, you are taking me from point one to point B, you are my driver.

2258
02:26:13,900 --> 02:26:19,420
Now the driver is not the one who is saluting the white uniform sir, coming forward and coming back. No.

2259
02:26:19,500 --> 02:26:22,820
But technically you are my driver. You are driving me from one place to another.

2260
02:26:22,900 --> 02:26:25,220
Sir come and sit in the front. I don't want to sit in the front.

2261
02:26:25,300 --> 02:26:29,620
Brother, it is a hot country. You are not driving the AC all day.

2262
02:26:29,700 --> 02:26:34,820
The margins of profit are very low. So you are in the heat. You know, there is body odor, ten things.

2263
02:26:34,900 --> 02:26:38,820
My legs are long. I don't have my legs in the front in the auto. I have to sit in the back.

2264
02:26:38,900 --> 02:26:41,480
And I want to lie down. I have a hobby of taking everything out of my pocket and spreading it.

2265
02:26:41,560 --> 02:26:48,480
I have two phones, one wallet, and back in the day, cigarette lighter, power bank, and all that stuff.

2266
02:26:48,560 --> 02:26:52,480
I used to sit in the front.

2267
02:26:52,560 --> 02:26:56,480
Or it was like, oh sir, it's my real estate job.

2268
02:26:56,560 --> 02:27:00,480
This is not my job. I do real estate work.

2269
02:27:00,560 --> 02:27:03,480
I get bored at work all day for a conversation.

2270
02:27:03,560 --> 02:27:06,560
Nowadays, you know, all the work is done on the phone.

2271
02:27:07,710 --> 02:27:11,630
It's better to go out in the city than to die in the city.

2272
02:27:11,710 --> 02:27:16,630
And meet educated people like you, have conversations, socialize.

2273
02:27:16,710 --> 02:27:21,630
This is the job of every person. Every Uber driver here does real estate.

2274
02:27:21,710 --> 02:27:23,630
And this is the job I am doing.

2275
02:27:23,710 --> 02:27:27,630
So that means he himself has assumed that the work is shameful.

2276
02:27:27,710 --> 02:27:32,630
So I'm not saying it's shameful work. I'm not saying that clean my shoes, do this, do that.

2277
02:27:32,710 --> 02:27:34,710
But that's the same thing.

2278
02:27:36,300 --> 02:27:38,920
So, they don't work here, everyone works outside.

2279
02:27:39,000 --> 02:27:46,000
You can forget about this thing. As long as you're making legit money, it's fine man. No problem.

2280
02:27:46,480 --> 02:27:48,379
What example can I give?

2281
02:27:48,459 --> 02:27:50,512
I was a waiter once.

2282
02:27:50,592 --> 02:27:53,124
I also got beaten up and abused.

2283
02:27:53,204 --> 02:27:53,704
Okay?

2284
